summary:
  The picture's kind is written after its address in every case, so for a
  moment the old kind stands beside the new address.

history:
  The kind and the address are two properties, and whatever reads them
  between the two writes sees a pair that never existed. Going from a
  song's cover to another record's sleeve, that pair is the sleeve under
  "track", which is the one word that lets a picture out to the lock
  screen. The kind is taken away before the address changes and given
  after it. This mutant writes the address first.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ArtworkEngine.qml

find:
          if (kind !== "track" || !url) albumArtKind = url ? kind : "";

replace:
          if (!url) albumArtKind = "";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_artworkengine.qml::test_the_kind_goes_with_its_picture_from_song_to_song.
  Line-neutral.
